{"obsah":"<p>The traditional event organised by the MTB &amp; Trial Mraveniště Říčany club under the leadership of Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček has grown somewhat since Pavel Hájek (former manager of the FORBIKES trade fair) joined. This year the programme was expanded, the event returned to a two-day format (as in the days of hosting international UCI C1 races) and an Expo zone was added.</p>\n\n<p>Big plans, demanding preparation – but the fate of outdoor events is always the roulette called weather. Šlapačky really got a taste of it this year. On the Monday before the race a storm arrived that completely destroyed the Tehov pump track. Thanks to the municipality of Tehov and Michal Maroši, a group of people was found who restored it almost to its original state, which – had it lasted – would have guaranteed a beautifully groomed track. Unfortunately, on Friday evening and practically all of Saturday all hell broke loose in Říčany and Tehov. The rain only stopped late on Saturday afternoon. The pump track was again practically half destroyed. But every event organiser knows you have to fight for success. So repairs to the pump track went on late into the night, with the promised warmer, sunny Sunday in prospect. Fortunately, it came.</p>\n\n<p>Practically most of Saturday's disciplines were moved to Sunday in a limited form. First to start was the rescheduled kids' Trial race, where spectators could admire the art of overcoming obstacles performed by the youngest kids from the club and guests. The race was ridden under modified rules that motivate riders to complete the whole section more than the current official rules do.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Because of the schedule the race was run quickly, and some riders could jump straight into the kids' MTB XC races, which were very physically demanding as the terrain slowly dried out. Parents cheered and the kids didn't give away a centimetre. The difficulty was reflected in the number of riders who gave up in the high humidity and heat – but hats off to them for finding the courage to race in these conditions.</p>\n\n<p>Next came the adults' Trial exhibition race, which was something of a Trial celebration. Four generations of Trial riders faced each other in one race. Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček, 10-time Czech Elite champion, against his master, multiple world champion Martin Šimůnek, who after almost 10 years of riding exhibitions tried racing again. As if that weren't enough, local native, Czech champion and Vlasta's student Petr Jeřicha also returned after 5 years. The circle was completed by Matouš Balík, Lukáš Valný and other guys from the club. Victory across all course difficulties went to Petr Jeřicha ahead of Martin and Vlasta. The latter took the win in the Elite category and the Trial record. The bunny hop contest was won by Lukáš Valný.</p>\n\n<p>While the adults' Trial was still going, training started on the pump track, which had dried a little. Pump track training had to be banned all morning. Conditions were the same for all riders, and although the track was slow and physically demanding, there were lots of great performances in the battles for fat prize money, trophies and medals.</p>\n\n<p>This year more than 115 riders started at the event, lots of fans came, and even more were unfortunately put off by the weather. You'll be able to watch footage from the event on ČT Déčko, or on the Trialshow and Bikeskills team YouTube channels once the edit is finished.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>We look forward to seeing you at next year's edition – hopefully the weather order will work out this time..</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/zN-Ku0RD3BQ\n</div></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_124353_resized.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_124353_resized.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-209639\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_130030_resized-1.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_130030_resized-1.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-209638\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_124652_resized.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_124652_resized.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-209637\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_122325_resized.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2F20220626_122325_resized.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-209636\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2Fcyklo-akce-3-scaled.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2022%2F07%2Fcyklo-akce-3-scaled.webp?alt=m